        "text_Ub47yL": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-md",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>In a dedicated air purifier, the filter faces consistent demands. In a 3-in-1 unit, the filter works across three different modes: heating, cooling, and purification, which means varying stress levels and wear patterns. Intelligent filter monitoring that tracks actual usage and pollution levels (rather than just replacing filters on a calendar schedule) becomes particularly valuable. You want to know exactly when replacement is needed, not guess and risk using a saturated filter or replacing filters prematurely.</p><h2>When Does a 3-in-1 Unit Make Sense?</h2><p>A 3-in-1 heater purifier is a practical choice if space efficiency is important and you want all three capabilities in one device. This works well for:</p><ul><li>Bedrooms where you want heating in winter, plus clean air year-round</li><li>Guest rooms or home offices with limited floor space</li><li>Smaller apartments where multiple appliances aren't feasible, particularly rooms around 175-350 square feet</li><li>Anyone who wants temperature control and air quality without managing separate devices</li></ul><p>For smaller rooms and apartments, a compact<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/3in1-air-purifier-t10i\"> 3-in-1 designed for 175 square feet</a> offers flexibility without taking up much floor space. If you have a larger bedroom or office around 350 square feet, a<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/3in1-air-purifier-t20i-1\"> more robust unit</a> makes sense to ensure adequate heating and purification coverage.</p><p>However, if air purification is your main priority and heating is secondary, a dedicated air purifier will give you more powerful performance. If you have a large living space where you need serious purification capability and separate temperature control, dedicated units might serve you better.</p><p>The critical distinction: a well-engineered 3-in-1 doesn't ask you to compromise on purification performance to get the heating feature. All three functions should work effectively, not force you to choose between them.</p><h2>What to Look For in a 3-in-1 Unit</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_KJNbEV": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
